You are helping build a platform for Rewa Supari Art.
This is a cultural heritage platform, not a generic store.
Project root is supari-art/.
Stack: Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, MongoDB, Mongoose,
NextAuth, Cloudinary, Razorpay, Stripe, Framer Motion, Resend.
Always use TypeScript with proper types from /types/index.ts.
Always use App Router patterns — never Pages Router.
Use server components by default, client components only when needed.
Phase 1: homepage uses placeholders only — wire to API in Phase 2.
Color palette: #3D2B1F #F5ECD7 #C8860A #FAF7F2 #D4A017.
Typography: Playfair Display for headings, Inter for body.
Design is premium, museum-like, story-driven — never generic e-commerce.
Every component should feel like it is presenting something rare and precious.
Artisan stories and craft process should be present throughout — not just
on dedicated pages.
Always add 'use client' directive when using hooks or browser APIs.
Use Framer Motion for entrance animations on all major sections.
Images always via next/image with proper alt text describing the craft.
MongoDB connection via lib/mongodb.ts singleton pattern.
Never use any as a type.
Environment variables: MONGODB_URI, NEXTAUTH_SECRET, CLOUDINARY_*,
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID, RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET, STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, RESEND_API_KEY.
